PARITY (web is THE spec — reproduced verbatim, not "corrected")
  • All 8 tiles in source order: Charger Power / Voltage / Current / Energy Added /
    Charging State / Battery Level / Charge Rate / Range Added, each with its web em-dash
    (`!= null ? formatted : '—'`) fallback and its MetricCard accent (green/cyan/purple).
  • Verbatim quirks preserved: Charger Power = `${fmtNumber(charger_power_w)} kW` (raw watts
    + "kW" suffix); Energy Added = `${fmtNumber(charge_energy_added_wh)} kWh` (raw Wh + "kWh").
    Battery Level = `${fmtNumber}%` with NO separating space. (covenant #2/#9 — no drift.)
  • Charge Rate = formatSpeed(range_added_meters_per_hour / 3600): metres-of-range/hour ÷3600
    → m/s → user km/h|mph (precision 0). Range Added = formatDistance(range_added_meters):
    SI metres → km(÷1000)|mi(÷1609.344) (precision 1). fmtNumber precision = decimal_precision
    ?? 2; distance/speed fall back to 1/0 when unset (web resolvePrecision reproduced exactly).
  • States widened to the full P4 leaf envelope: loading / empty (web EmptyState) / error
    (QueryError peer + retry) / data / stale + offline (freshness chip + banner + one-shot
    stale auto-refresh). i18n via the P1/S10 facade (no English literals in Swift). VoiceOver
    labels on every tile + container; Dynamic Type; Reduce-Motion via TSSkeleton/TSFadeIn.
  • Collision discipline: the existing dashboard ChargingTelemetryWidget OWNS every
    `ChargingTelemetry*` type name in the module, so EVERY type here is prefixed
    `ChargingTelemetrySection*` (verified collision-free). This is the very class of
    duplicate-type collision that breaks StateTimeline below — deliberately avoided here.

